  "description": "A stealth HTTP client library for .NET that bypasses Cloudflare / DataDome and most TLS handshake security measures using advanced browser TLS fingerprinting. The Go tls-client engine runs out-of-process as a loopback-only sidecar (auto-downloaded on first use, binds 127.0.0.1 so there is no network exposure and no firewall prompt), so it never crashes the host on Linux and needs no Node.js. Supports multiple browser profiles (Chrome, Firefox, Safari), randomized TLS extension order, header-order control, cookie management, and proxies.",
